course: dictionary
lesson: 2430
title: Dabble: trying things out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To dabble means to try something a little, not very seriously. You can dabble in painting or dabble with the guitar to see if you like it. «Dabble in» means having a go at a hobby.
explain: Dabble also means to move your hands or feet gently in water, splashing a bit. Think of a child who dabbles her toes in a stream on a warm day. The water is the clue: the movement is light and gentle.
explain: Ducks dabble too. «A duck that tips upside down with its tail up is dabbling, reaching for plants and small animals just below the surface.» Here dabble means feeding in shallow water. Diving ducks go right under, so dabbling is the shallower kind.
fact: Dabble is a verb: I dabble, she dabbles, they dabbled, dabbling.
fact: A person who dabbles in a hobby can be called a dabbler.
fact: «Dabble in» means to have a go at a hobby without being very serious about it.
fact: «Dabble your feet» means to move your feet gently in water, splashing a bit.
fact: Dabbling ducks, like mallards, tip forward to reach food in shallow water.
exercise: «I only want to dabble in painting, not become a real artist.» What does dabble mean here? | Paint the walls of a house | *Try it a little, as a hobby | Sell paintings in a big shop | Paint very seriously every day
exercise: Mia sat on the side of the pool and dabbled her feet in the water. What does dabbled mean? | Dived right under the water | Dried her feet on a towel | *Moved her feet gently in the water, splashing a bit | Swam fast across the pool
exercise: Ducks tip upside down with their tails up to dabble for food. Where do they find the food? | Deep at the bottom of the sea | On the grass, far from any water | Way up in the trees | *Just below the surface of shallow water
test: Which word means a person who dabbles in a hobby? | *dabbler | dabbling | dabble | dabbles
test: Which sentence uses dabble to mean splashing gently in water? | Dabble is a verb with four forms | The duck dived right under the lake | *The toddler dabbled his hands in the warm bath | Mum dabbled in cooking on Sundays
exam: What does dabble mean when a duck tips up to feed? | Dive deep under the water | *Tip forward to reach food in shallow water | Sleep on the bank | Fly away over the trees
